  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The v2 .golangci.yml enables lll at 100 with a house-width comment, the hook adds a Go branch in the existing filter/have/note style that lints the staged files' package directories, skips with a notice when golangci-lint is absent, leaves Go-free commits unaffected, and AGENTS.md gains a Go row; the only slip is that gofmt is not run directly on the staged files but only via golangci-lint's formatters, so a missing golangci-lint also drops the format check, and package-level linting can block on unstaged files."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 3,
        "rationale": "No workflow was added and other languages' configs and the Markdown/YAML opt-outs are untouched, but the agent edited main.go to add a package comment, which fails go-sources-unchanged and caps restraint at 3."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply states the check lives only in the local hook, that no lint workflow exists so no CI step was added and why, flags the stale code-quality.yml claim in the hook header, and clearly separates what was run (golangci-lint, go test, manual hook probes) from what was not (config verify, ShellCheck, shfmt, yamllint), only lightly implying rather than stating that contributors without golangci-lint commit unchecked."
      }
    ],
